Any assignment of an element to every neighbourhood system and every approximable endomap, such that the assigned element is a fixed point and the assignment is uniform along maps that preserve bottom and intertwine the endomaps, agrees with the least fixed point.

The least fixed point of the given endomap is fixed by that endomap. The value of the assignment on the restriction to the relativized system below that least fixed point is a fixed point of the restriction, hence equals the restriction of the least fixed point to itself. Uniformity along the inclusion of the relativized system, which preserves bottom and intertwines the restriction with the original endomap, transports this value to the assigned element. The elementwise action of the inclusion and the embedding of a restriction identify that transported value with the least fixed point.
